 "content_notes": "Tone: absurd and ironic, never mocking. Anna Ayala and Jaime Plascencia are real people who pleaded guilty and were sentenced (2006): drawn ONLY as dark silhouettes tagged NOT A LIKENESS. The co-worker who lost the fingertip was never charged: not named, not shown. The finger is never shown: the bowl is half covered by a napkin and the evidence bag's contents are blurred; no injury is shown (the tailgate shot has nobody near it). Wendy's is named only in narration and plain text: no logo, no mascot, no packaging or uniform artwork; the restaurant, bowl, takeaway box, uniforms and the asphalt yard are generic illustrations. The restaurant was the victim of the hoax and nothing suggests otherwise. No dialogue is invented. Facts verified 2026-10-17.",
